Bluetooth: Advertising

### Android Background Execution

Follow the current Android background execution restrictions.

Evaluate Companion Device Manager APIs and appropriate foreground-service use.

Use the connectedDevice foreground-service type when its requirements are satisfied.

Use phoneCall only when the application meets the documented eligibility requirements, such as ROLE_DIALER or MANAGE_OWN_CALLS.

Use microphone only during an eligible microphone session.

Use dataSync only for appropriate transfer operations and comply with newer Android execution time limits.

Do not declare all foreground-service types merely to keep a process alive.

Do not claim the service can run forever.

Implement:

- Proper notification channels.
- User-controlled service start/stop.
- Process recreation handling.
- Connection recovery.
- Graceful cleanup.
- WakeLock timeout.
- Service lifecycle logging.

The service must not automatically attempt restricted background operations following device boot.

